---
import Page from '../layouts/Page.astro';
import { SITE } from '../config';
const updated = 'October 17, 2026';
---
<Page title="Privacy Policy" description="How BlenderHacks handles your information.">
  <p class="muted">Last updated: {updated}</p>
  <p>This policy explains what information {SITE.name} ({SITE.url}) collects and how it's used.</p>
  <h2>Information we collect</h2>
  <p>We don't ask you to create an account and we don't collect names or email addresses unless you choose to email us. Like most websites, our hosting provider may automatically log basic technical data (such as IP address, browser type, and pages requested) to keep the site running and secure.</p>
  <h2>Advertising and cookies</h2>
  <p>We use Google AdSense to show ads. Third-party vendors, including Google, use cookies to serve ads based on your prior visits to this website or other websites. Google's use of advertising cookies enables it and its partners to serve ads to you based on your visits to this site and/or other sites on the Internet.</p>
  <p>You can opt out of personalized advertising by visiting <a href="https://adssettings.google.com/" rel="noopener">Google Ads Settings</a>, or opt out of some third-party vendors' use of cookies for personalized advertising at <a href="https://www.aboutads.info/choices/" rel="noopener">aboutads.info</a>. To learn more, see <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/ads" rel="noopener">how Google uses information from sites that use its services</a>.</p>
  <h2>Affiliate links</h2>
  <p>When you click an affiliate link (for example, to Amazon), the destination site may set cookies so it can credit us for any qualifying purchase. Those cookies are governed by that site's own privacy policy, such as <a href="https://www.amazon.com/gp/help/customer/display.html?nodeId=GX7NJQ4ZB8MHFRNJ" rel="noopener">Amazon's Privacy Notice</a>.</p>
  <h2>Analytics</h2>
  <p>We use Google Analytics to understand how visitors use the site, such as which pages are read, how long visits last and roughly where visitors come from (country or region). Google Analytics uses cookies and collects data such as your device and browser type, pages viewed and an approximate location derived from your IP address. We use this information only in aggregate to improve the site. You can read <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites" rel="noopener">how Google uses data from sites that use its services</a>, and opt out with the <a href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout" rel="noopener">Google Analytics opt-out browser add-on</a>.</p>
  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>Questions about this policy? Email <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>.</p>
</Page>
